From: rgslide-linux <mainline@rgslide>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sprd: add Unisoc UMS9620 (qogirn6pro) DPU R6P0 and DSI handoff support

Enable mainline DRM KMS scanout on the Anbernic RG Slide (UMS9620 / T820):
- Fix Linux 6.18 drmm_universal_plane_alloc() / drmm_crtc_alloc_with_planes()
  by dropping legacy .destroy callbacks on managed plane and CRTC funcs.
- Register a lightweight genpd provider for "sprd,vpu-pd" so 31000000.dpu and
  31300000.dsi satisfy their stock DT power-domains dependency without blocking.
- Bind only dpu0 (31000000.dpu) + dsi0 (31300000.dsi) on qogirn6pro so
  display-subsystem does not stall waiting for unbound dpu1 (DisplayPort).
- Add DPU R6P0 register map (0x08 CTRL, 0x2c LAY_EN mask, 0x40 layer stride,
  0x250/0x254/0x258 IRQ regs, BIT(4) VSYNC, BIT(18) UPDATE_DONE) in handoff
  mode preserving the live LK DSI/DPHY/FT8201P 1280x960 pipeline.
- Add qogirn6pro-dsi-host handoff connector exposing the FT8201P 1280x960@60Hz
  mode and call drm_client_setup() for fbdev/fbcon support.

